---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import ToVerify from '../../components/ToVerify.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Utility Transition"
  description="What residents of the Village of Midvale need to know about the transition of water service to Aqua Ohio."
  eyebrow="Resources"
  intro="The Village's water service has transitioned to Aqua Ohio under a 2024 Asset Purchase Agreement that closed in Q1 2025."
>
  <ToVerify note="Specific dates, the Aqua Ohio service number, and final payment instructions need to be confirmed before publishing." />

  <section class="prose-village max-w-prose">
    <h2>Why this transition?</h2>
    <p>
      Operating a small public water system requires meeting an evolving set of
      Ohio EPA standards while also funding ongoing infrastructure investment
      &mdash; a stretch for villages of Midvale's size. After evaluating
      alternatives, the Village entered into an Asset Purchase Agreement with
      Aqua Ohio in August 2024, with the transaction closing in Q1 2025.
    </p>

    <h2>Will my bill change?</h2>
    <p>
      You will receive billing from Aqua Ohio rather than the Village. Aqua
      Ohio's rates are regulated by the Public Utilities Commission of Ohio
      (PUCO). For specifics, contact Aqua Ohio customer service.
    </p>

    <h2>Will my service change?</h2>
    <p>
      Day-to-day water service should remain reliable. Aqua Ohio is responsible
      for repairs, infrastructure investment, and water quality compliance.
    </p>

    <h2>Who do I call for water emergencies now?</h2>
    <p>
      Call <strong>Aqua Ohio</strong> (number to be added once verified). For
      drainage problems on village streets, contact the Village Streets Department.
    </p>

    <h2>What about my final village water payment?</h2>
    <p>
      Instructions for residents who had a final balance with the Village water
      utility at the time of transition will be added once verified.
    </p>

    <h2>Where can I learn more?</h2>
    <p>
      Aqua Ohio's customer service page:
      <a href="https://www.aquawater.com/about-us/our-states/ohio" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aquawater.com (Ohio)</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Public Utilities Commission of Ohio:
      <a href="https://www.puco.ohio.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">puco.ohio.gov</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
